-~> engine: the way Linkz runs lizard code it loads or is given (the
-~> libraries, a drawing, the editor): on the bytecode VM, or on the
-~> tree-walking evaluator when LINKZ_ENGINE is "tree", the fallback if the VM
-~> ever misbehaves. Both give the same results; the VM is several times faster.

-~> The engine option of lizard.run: "vm" or "evaluator".
function engine_name() {
  if (os.env("LINKZ_ENGINE") == "tree") {
    return "evaluator"
  }
  "vm"
}
